# Code owners: the maintainer owns the high-risk paths, the ones that decide what CI
# checks, what the app may do in its sandbox, what gets built and released, which
# crates it depends on, and what agents are told. A pull request that touches one
# requests his review. Everything else has no owner.
#
# Patterns use .gitignore syntax: a leading `/` anchors to the repository root, a
# name without `/` matches at any depth, and `*` does not cross `/`.

# CI and release workflows, and this file itself.
/.github/                           @Tim-van-Oudheusden

# Flatpak manifests and their lint exceptions (sandbox permissions, runtime,
# modules), the RPM and DEB recipes, and the scripts CI and releases run: the
# version and manifest checks, crate vendoring, release notes and smoke tests.
/build-aux/                         @Tim-van-Oudheusden

# The build: every meson.build (the nested ones drive cargo and register the
# tests CI runs) and the build options.
meson.build                         @Tim-van-Oudheusden
/meson.options                      @Tim-van-Oudheusden

# Dependencies and the lint and format policy: every crate's Cargo.toml, the
# lock file, and the clippy and rustfmt settings.
Cargo.toml                          @Tim-van-Oudheusden
/Cargo.lock                         @Tim-van-Oudheusden
/clippy.toml                        @Tim-van-Oudheusden
/rustfmt.toml                       @Tim-van-Oudheusden

# Release notes and app metadata, and stored settings.
/data/*.metainfo.xml.in             @Tim-van-Oudheusden
/data/*.gschema.xml.in              @Tim-van-Oudheusden

# Agent instructions and the AI disclosure.
/AGENTS.md                          @Tim-van-Oudheusden
/AI_DISCLOSURE.md                   @Tim-van-Oudheusden
/CLAUDE.md                          @Tim-van-Oudheusden
